% meaning that Hercules exploits these core components to provide diverse directions,
In this case and many others, providing prior knowledge in prompts can help LLMs reduce unspecificity in their responses, leading to more focused, specific search directions. To achieve this, we propose the zero-shot CAP method, which can abstract the core components from the top-$k$ heuristics in the current population without additional guidance. Because the core components are essential for heuristic performance \citep{7339682, liu2024evolution}, leveraging them enables LLMs to provide more specific search directions. As shown in Figure~\ref{figcap}(b), the suggested direction \textit{``Normalize penalties relative to overall distance"} may lead to more effective heuristic generation. In addition, CAP abstracts the core components once per iteration, instead of abstracting distinct components separately for crossover and elitist mutation operators. Consequently, this approach helps prevent a significant increase in context and generation token costs compared to RP (see Table~\ref{tabsearchreport} in the experiment section). 
