Autonomous robots and cobots in smart factories increasingly rely on digital twins and secure communication to synchronize operations. Emerging frameworks propose quantum-secured control planes using entanglement-based authentication and teleportation-assisted state synchronization~\cite{Ghosh2024Industry60,Senapati2025Battery}. These designs aim to prevent control hijacks and spoofing of autonomous units by leveraging QKD protocols embedded within digital twin architectures. Vision transformers and AI-driven simulations further enhance the fidelity and temporal coherence of quantum robotics operations~\cite{Kovari2025VisionTransformers}.

