Transactional APIs in fintech are being redesigned with quantum communication overlays to ensure forward secrecy, entanglement-based authentication, and minimal cryptographic overhead. Mosteanu and Faccia~\cite{mosteanu2021quantumapi} propose a layered framework where QKD-derived session keys are dynamically exchanged between payment processors, enabling entropy-backed validation of transactions without relying on legacy TLS stacks. These APIs are compatible with digital wallets, CBDCs, and smart contract triggers, enhancing resilience in decentralized finance (DeFi) environments.

