Fraud detection systems powered by quantum entropy sources are increasingly embedded within blockchain infrastructures. Weinberg and Faccia~\cite{weinberg2024quantumfraud} introduce quantum-enhanced fraud detection protocols where entangled signatures detect anomalous behavior and prevent man-in-the-middle exploits. Quantum blockchains offer post-quantum compliance and transactional transparency without compromising speed or cost-effectiveness by combining QKD and entropy hashing in consensus protocols.

