High-frequency trading (HFT) demands ultra-low latency and secure communication between geographically distributed financial nodes. Lee et al.~\cite{lee2022quantumfintech} highlight the integration of real-time QKD channels in HFT exchanges to protect proprietary trading algorithms from being intercepted or reverse-engineered. Entangled links between data centers and quantum routers enable per-trade encryption, immediate key revocation, and synchronization without introducing measurable delays in trading pipelines.



