Quantum testbeds offer physical and virtualized environments where researchers can evaluate entanglement protocols, quantum channel behaviors, and OSI stack interoperability. The DOE ASCR Testbeds Program~\cite{lougovski2023ascr} supports experimentation with multi-node quantum infrastructures and hybrid classical–quantum integration layers. These testbeds facilitate reproducible benchmarking, device calibration, and error propagation modeling critical to early-stage protocol deployment. They also support interoperability testing between vendor-specific qubit architectures and distributed nodes.

