Satellite-based telemetry for environmental data gathering is evolving with the integration of quantum-secured channels. Distributed quantum telemetry frameworks are being evaluated by agencies like NASA for high-fidelity climate tracking, where QKD-secured links are used to safeguard observational payloads~\cite{Kitching2023NASAQSensing}. These systems help avoid falsification or interception of environmental data across transnational infrastructures. Rossi et al.~\cite{Rossi2025PlanetaryScience} also discuss in-situ planetary observatories leveraging quantum methane detectors and entanglement-based data downlink.

