Table~\ref{tab:execution_cost} presents a comparison of the execution cost for the three models. GPT-4VV processes the dataset in approximately 6 hours and 48 minutes at a cost of \textdollar{}5.41, and BLIP-2 is even more efficient, running in roughly 31 minutes and 34 seconds at a modal cost of \textdollar{}0.65. In stark contrast, MILS requires a staggering runtime of 116 hours and 40 minutes, incurring a cost of \textdollar{}291.66. These figures underscore the heavy computational overhead of MILS's iterative approach.

