  More generally, given any simplex $\spx \subseteq \Rspace^d$ (not necessarily in $\Del{P,\alpha}$), we
  define $S(\spx,\alpha) = \bigcap_{p \in \spx} \partial B(p,\alpha)$.
  Assuming that $\Conv{\spx} \subseteq \Rspace^d \setminus \MA{\M}$ and
  $S(\spx,\alpha) \neq \emptyset$, we associate to $\spx$ and any $x \in \Conv{\spx}$
  the highest point of $S(\spx,\alpha)$ in direction $\normal
