\subsection{Error Estimates}
We present the error estimates for \eqref{fully-discret-scheme}. To do this, we first derive the error equations, which will subsequently be used in Theorem~\ref{error-estimates thm}, with appropriate choices of test functions, to establish the estimates. 

\medskip \noindent 
\noindent {\bf Error equations}

 \noindent 
A linear combination of the equations in the system \eqref{weak form}}, evaluated at $t=t_{n-1}$, $t=t_n,$ and $t=t_{n+1}$, for $n=1,2,\cdots, N-1$,  yields
\begin{subequations}
\begin{align}
    (u_{tt}^{n,1/4},Qv_h)&+a_0 (\nabla u_{tt}^{n,1/4},\nabla Qv_h)\nonumber  \\
    &+d_0(\nabla ^2 u^{n,1/4}, \nabla^2 Qv_h) -\alpha (\nabla \theta^{n,1/4}, \nabla Qv_h)
    -\beta (\nabla p^{n,1/4}, \nabla Qv_h) =(f^{n,1/4},Qv_h), \label{u^n}\\
    a_1(\theta_t^{n+1/2}, \psi_h)&-\gamma (p_t^{n+1/2}, \psi_h)+b_1(\theta^{n+1/2},\psi_h) \nonumber
\\&+c_1 (\nabla \theta^{n+1/2},\nabla \psi_h) +\alpha (\nabla u_t^{n+1/2}, \nabla \psi_h)=(\phi^{n+1/2},\psi_h), \label{theta^n} \\
    a_2 (p_t^{n+1/2},q_h)&-\gamma (\theta_t^{n+1/2},q_h)+\kappa (\nabla p^{n+1/2},\nabla q_h)+\beta (\nabla u_t^{n+1/2},\nabla q_h)=(g^{n+1/2},q_h),\label{p^n}
    \end{align}
    \end{subequations}
    $\text{for all } v_h \in V_h $ and $\psi_h,q_h \in  W_h$, 
   where as earlier we have used  Range$(Q) \subset H^2_0(\Omega)$ and $W_h \subset H^1_0(\Omega)$ .

