% The extent of this effect is influenced by the teacher model's angular distance, \( \theta^s_{i,j} \). 
% For negative pairs, the margin is subtracted, increasing the angular distance and reducing the similarity.
% In both cases, the margin space is determined by the teacher model, allowing the LLM to effectively learn relationships between positive and negative pairs as well as the relative distances within pairs from the output representations of the small model.
% In both cases, the margin space is determined by the teacher model, allowing the LLM to effectively learn relationships between positive and negative pairs as well as the relative distances within pairs from the output representations of the small model.
