\subsubsection{One-to-all shortest beer path on transformed graph}

To compute shortest temporal paths from $x\in V$, it suffices to run Dijkstra's algorithm in $\tilde{G}$ from a dummy vertex $x'$, connected via directed edges of weight 0 to every $(x, t) \in \tilde{V}_{\text{out}}(x)$ s.t. $\ t_\alpha \leq t \leq t_\omega$, thus representing all valid departure times from $x$ \cite{Path_Wu}.

We modify Dijkstra's algorithm by storing a $3$-valued flag for each $(v,t)\in \tilde{G}$ and updating it in the same manner described in the previous subsection. This algorithm visits each $(v,t) \in \tilde{G}$ at most twice, thus calculating SBP distances in $\bigO(M\log(M))$ time.

