Although these methods have advanced 3D generation in speed and quality,
the unsatisfying performance of multi-view generation and the growing demands for higher mesh quality have led researchers to focus increasingly on the development of native 3D generation methods~\citep{liu2023one2345++, gupta20233dgen, chen2024primx, Wang2023rodin, ren2024xcube,hong20243dtopia}.
3DShape2Vecset~\citep{3dshape2vecset} and CLAY~\citep{zhang2024clay} exploit latent vector sets as representation, significantly enhancing the expressiveness of the latent space.
