In our experiments, we compare our method with state-of-the-art image-to-3D methods from two categories. (1) \textbf{Large reconstruction models}~\citep{LRM, PF-LRM, instant3d, wang2024crm, tang2024lgm} exploit a neural network to map sparse views into 3D representations, including InstantMesh~\citep{xu2024instantmesh}, TripoSR~\citep{TripoSR2024} and MeshFormer~\citep{liu2024meshformer}. To be clear, the results of MeshFormer are obtained through their official demo, since has not been open-sourced.
(2) \textbf{Native 3D generation models}~\citep{liu2023one2345++, 3dshape2vecset, zhang2024clay} compress discrete 3D meshes into a continuous and compact latent space using a 3D auto-encoder, followed by a diffusion model trained on this latent space to achieve 3D generation, including LN3Diff~\citep{lan2024ln3diff}, 3DTopia-XL~\citep{chen2024primx}, and CraftsMan~\citep{li2024craftsman}.

\subtitle{Qualitative results.}
We present a qualitative comparison between our method and large reconstruction models in the upper part of \fref{fig:comp_lrm}. Our approach significantly outperforms others in generating high-quality geometry. Specifically, our method excels at producing complex structures from images, such as the mouth of the alien and the file sorter, where large reconstruction models struggle. Additionally, large reconstruction models often suffer from poor multi-view generation outcomes, resulting in lower quality when reconstructing details that require multi-view consistency.
% 我们在图x中展示了我们的方法与之前的3D native generation的qualitative comparison, where我们的方法显著的优于其他的方法by a significant margin。我们注意到其他的方法倾向于生成对称且过于简单的几何结构，并且和输入图片之间存在明显的不相似性。而我们的方法利用分析得出的两种data augmentation很大程度上缓解了这种问题，这种相似性增强了shape增强的可控性，而且为后续的texturing减小了gap。对于3DTopia-XL，其应用的显式表示相较于我们使用的point-to-shape auto-encoder压缩率较低，导致其虽然使用了数倍于我们的训练成本，但依然和我们的生成效果有较大差距.
% We demonstrate in \fref{fig:comp_native} a qualitative comparison between other 3D native generation methods, where our method significantly outperforms other methods by a large margin. We notice that other methods tend to generate symmetrical and overly simplistic geometric structures, and there is a clear dissimilarity between these structures and the input images. Our method, utilizing two types of data augmentation derived from analysis, largely alleviates this issue. This similarity enhances the controllability of shape generation and makes subsequent texturing much easier. For 3DTopia-XL, the explicit representation it employs yields a lower compression rate compared to the point-to-shape auto-encoder. As a consequence, despite incurring much higher training costs, it still exhibits a substantial disparity in generation performance when compared with our method.
In the lower part of \fref{fig:comp_lrm}, we provide a qualitative comparison with 3D native generation methods. As we mentioned earlier, previous native 3D generation models are limited by data and the expressive power of the autoencoder, often resulting in overly simple and symmetrical geometries that significantly differ from the reference images. 
Our method, leveraging the proposed two data augmentations, effectively addresses this issue. This image-shape alignment enhances the controllability of shape generation and simplifies subsequent texturing. 
% \shit{For 3DTopia-XL, its explicit representation results in a lower compression rate compared to the point-to-shape auto-encoder. Consequently, despite higher training costs, \approach still outperforms 3DTopia-XL by a large margin.}

