\subsection{Ablations}

\subtitle{Render-enhanced auto-encoder.}
% 为了评估使用render loss的重要性，我们在不加入render loss情况下训练了一个auto-encoder来和我们的render-enhanced autoencoder比较，其比较如图x的上半部分所示。render-enhanced autoencoder的表现显著的好于只有BCE loss训练出的auto-encoder，尤其是在一些高频的细节上，例如触手上的吸盘和表带上的缝隙。
To evaluate the significance of incorporating render loss in the point-to-shape auto-encoder, we trained a variant without render-based perceptual loss and compared it to our render-enhanced version, as illustrated in the upper part of \fref{fig:ablation}. The render-enhanced auto-encoder performs markedly better, particularly in capturing high-frequency details such as the suckers on tentacles and the gaps in watch bands. In \tref{tab:autoencoder}, we also demonstrate through quantitative results the superiority of the render-enhanced auto-encoder compared to 3DShape2VecSet and the no-render-loss variant.

\subtitle{Geomtric alignment augmentation.}
% 为了验证rotation augmentation的作用，我们在一个相对较小的网络上进行了300 epoch的训练，尽管得到的结果相较于我们的full模型质量较差，我们相信足以说明rotation augmentation的作用。很明显，没有加入rotation augmentation的diffusion模型倾向于产生对称的物体，而我们的模型生成的shape可以很好地图像align，大大地增强了diffusion模型的可控性
% To validate the effect of geometric alignment augmentation, we trained a smaller diffusion UNet without geometric alignment augmentation for 300 epochs. Although the results are of lower quality compared to our full model, we believe they are sufficient to demonstrate the impact of rotation augmentation. The comparison is shown in the lower left part of \fref{fig:ablation}. Clearly, the diffusion model trained without geometric alignment augmentation tends to generate symmetric objects, whereas our model produces shapes that align well with the images, significantly enhancing the controllability of the diffusion model.
To validate the impact of geometric alignment augmentation, we trained a variant without this augmentation for 300 epochs as an ablation study. The comparison is presented in the lower left part of \fref{fig:ablation}. Evidently, the diffusion model trained without geometric alignment augmentation tends to generate symmetric objects, whereas our model produces shapes that align well with the input images, significantly enhancing the model's controllability.
% 由于train一个diffusion需要的计算量过于庞大，我们在一个相对较小的网络上进行了有限steps的训练，尽管得到的结果相较于我们的full模型质量较差，我们相信由于说明我们提出的augmentatin的方式是足够的。我们在图X中展示了在有rotation augmentation和没有rotation augmentation的情况下训练出的diffusion模型的表现

\subtitle{Generative rendering augmentation.}
% 为了评估generative rendering augmentation对于image-to-shape diffusion training 的作用，我们在没有generative rendering augmentation的setting下训练了一个小模型，其效果如图x右下部分所示。没有generative rendering augmentation训练出的模型在面对图像中光照效果是表现不佳，无法通过光照效果判断出物体的几何结构，并且在面对真实物体时泛化能力很差。这些实验现象表明了generative rendering augmentation提升了模型在面对光照效果和面对真实图像时的表现
% To evaluate the effect of generative rendering augmentation on image-to-shape diffusion training, we trained a small model without generative rendering augmentation, as shown in the lower right part of \fref{fig:ablation}. 
% The model trained without generative rendering augmentation performs poorly when dealing with lighting effects in images and struggles to infer the geometric structure of objects from lighting\shit{(such as determining the shape of a doll's head or the blender)}.
