We evaluated the structural quality of generated content from both local and global perspectives.

\paragraph{Section-Level Structure} This dimension assesses the internal coherence and logical flow of individual sections and subsections, following the rubric proposed in \textsc{AutoSurvey}. A score of 1 indicates disorganized or incoherent content, while a score of 5 denotes a tightly structured and logically consistent organization with smooth transitions. After evaluation, the score is linearly scaled to a 0–100 range. The full rubric is provided in Table~\ref{table:struct_eval}.

